<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka T-bill yields rise at weekly auction.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka T-bill yields rise at weekly auction.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yields of three-, six- and 12-month Sri Lankan treasury bills rose at Wednesday's auctions from those of last week, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>		  bids received   bids accepted   avg yield</p>
<p>    3 months     2,722	     2,622	  17.27 (17.08)</p>
<p>    6 months     1,780	     1,735	  17.26 (17.15)</p>
<p>    12 months    1,006		 716	  17.40 (17.29)</p>
<p>The Central Bank said it purchased treasury bills totalling 579 million rupees.</p>
<p>NOTE - Bids in million rupees, yields in percent (previous week's yields in brackets). --Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
